28.. Considering the Duration of the Closure of the Second and Third Block of Main Street for Restaurant / Retail Use During the COVID-19 Pandemic  -  Action: substitute (Fail) Moved by Kim Carr {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 City Manager Oliver Chi presented a PowerPoint presentation entitled: Downtown Street Closures with slides titled: Background, Second Block of Main Street(3), Third Block of Main Street(3), Diagram of Current Setup With Street Closure, Potential Diagram of Setup if Street Reopened, Second Block of Main Street Update, Third Block of Main Street Update, City Council Action, Staff Recommendation, and Questions.\par
\par
Posey - 1 month ago 3rd block closed, transference of energy has not yet made it to 3rd block, feels water barriers less invasive and camouflaged.  Possibly utilize Live music element at both north and south end of blocks. Wants contingency plan - keep 3rd block closed to traffic.\par
\par
Delgleize - like to see 3rd block stay closed longer, need more time to gain popularity and gives business owner more opportunities.\par
\par
Hardy - concurred with Posey & Delgleize, agrees with entertainment suggestion.\par
\par
Carr - concurs with previous councilmember comments, would like to see 3rd block closed through Oct. 31 due to cooler weather concerns and more retail on the block and then re-evaluate.\par
\par
Peterson - Not enthusiastic keeping 3rd block closed due to types of businesses in area.  Prefer to hear from 3rd block businesses.\par
\par
Brenden - due to only partial re-opening of inside dining, feels outdoor dining needs to continue with street closure (especially on 2nd block) - wants to hear from BID Board, and would like to hear more residents opinion.\par
\par
Semeta - agrees water barriers need revising to not appear the 3rd block closed\par
\par
Posey - would like email report from CMgr to update council on improvements/progress. Over 80 emergency permits issued. \par
}


28.. Considering the Duration of the Closure of the Second and Third Block of Main Street for Restaurant / Retail Use During the COVID-19 Pandemic  -  Action: approved (Pass) Moved by Mike Posey
